<!--
  SlotCompositionProbe.rozie

  Phase 85 Plan 06 Task 3 (D5) — the ONE deliberately-nested composition
  fixture the corpus needed and never had: a conditional (`r-if`) containing
  a component reference, that component's slot filled with a scoped
  parameter (`#header="{ remaining, total }"`), and a loop (`r-for`) inside
  the fill body — with expressions at every level reading the loop alias,
  the slot parameter, and a `$props` sigil together. Every other probe in
  this corpus tests one of those constructs in isolation; every known
  failure of this generator has been a NESTING failure, one level off.

  Reuses `TodoList.rozie`'s existing scoped `header` slot — it exposes two
  scoped params, a computed remaining-count and a total — as the producer
  rather than adding a second new file.

  Two interpolations near the end are DELIBERATE NEGATIVE probes — they
  read the loop alias / slot parameter from OUTSIDE the scope that
  introduces them and are expected to NOT resolve at the TypeScript layer
  (`slotScope.test.ts` already established this "leak probe" pattern for
  the language-server test suite; here it proves the SAME boundary holds
  under real nesting, not just isolation). This is a Rozie-COMPILE-clean
  file — `compile()` does no JS-identifier resolution, so these negative
  probes cost nothing at the ROZIE level; they exist purely for the
  TypeScript-layer scope assertions in `probes.test.ts`.
-->

<rozie name="SlotCompositionProbe">

<components>
{
  TodoList: './TodoList.rozie',
}
</components>

<props>
{
  items: { type: Array, default: () => [] },
  label: { type: String, default: '' },
}
</props>

<template>
<div class="slot-composition-probe">
  <TodoList r-if="$props.items.length > 0" :items="$props.items">
    <template #header="{ remaining, total }">
      <ul class="composed">
        <li r-for="entry in $props.items" :key="entry.id">
          {{ entry.id + remaining + total + $props.label.length }}<!-- ^? -->
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="after-loop">{{ remaining }}{{ entry }}</p>
    </template>
  </TodoList>
  <p class="outside-fill">{{ remaining }}{{ entry }}</p>
</div>
</template>

</rozie>
